hes) - kinda of a paladin/combat cleric sort of deal<br /> Gundogs (dog, birds name it Gunners, lizards name it Shooters) - they like guns<br /> Torpedoes (cat; birds name it Duelists, lizards name it Gunslingers) mix of guns and stealth<br /> Mystic (cat; birds name it Soothsayers, lizards name it Magi) - spellcasters with a somewhat druid feel particularly as they relate to the sea<br /> Alkalist (lizard) - alchemist/potion makers that focus on salt<br /> Rimers (bird) bard style entertainers and cutthroats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":".  typo 05-22-2019, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T18:51:31-07:00","id":1313601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1245406-pirates-of-pugmire?p=1313598#post1313598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crusaders (dog; birds name it Troopers, lizards name it Dervishes) - kinda of a paladin/combat cleric sort of deal<br /> Gundogs (dog, birds name it Gunners, lizards name it Shooters) - they like guns<br /> Torpedoes (cat; birds name it Duelists, lizards name it Gunslighers) mix of guns and stealth<br /> Mystic (cat; birds name it Soothsayers, lizards name it Magi) - spellcasters with a somewhat druid feel particularly as they relate to the sea<br /> Alkalist (lizard) - alchemist/potion makers that focus on salt<br /> Rimers (bird) bard style entertainers and cutthroats.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the temptation needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T05:07:58-07:00","id":1313646,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Kickstarter, for those looking for the link, here it is:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/pirates-of-pugmire-a-realms-of-pugmire-tabletop-rpg/description\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...pg/description</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T19:29:14-07:00","id":1313968,"title":"","content":"I wonder why this one isn't attracting people as quickly as the others did though. Monarchies and Pugmire both blew past $40k in their first day. Three days in and Pirates just hit $20k.<br /> <br /> I mean, I get that the setting is somewhat more niche, but it's got plenty of player options and stuff. Two new playable races, six new classes. That's nerd candy, usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T21:48:48-07:00","id":1313988,"title":"","content":"I've heard that there is a level of diminishing returns on any game line to be expected. While Mau wasn't fully a new line it was standalone. This is the first &quot;big&quot; book in the Realms that isn't a standalone game. Also might be that the new Species aren't as popular as pets as Dogs or Cats. I really don't know. As I've mentioned before I've generally been kinda nutty for pirates so I really can't figure out what's slowing people.<br /> <br /> Gotta say, there was a moment where I was disappointed that the new Callings would be just using other Callings' knacks, but it was just a moment. As I started actually looking at how the new ones change up starting knacks it's actually really fucking elegant and the thoughts of what can be done with a Mystic as ship mage and navigator with Mancy to start and then Natural Explorer so they're never lost at sea. Or the fact that Torpedoes get Darkvision as a starting Knack? Only Calling to get that in the game as far as I can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T00:46:05-07:00","id":1314003,"title":"","content":"Am I only one that think that Torpedoes should be renamed Assasin's ( Creed ) for this game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/025/148/323/0c458118288dd783dbfc5e7fc7c5055a_original.jpg?ixlib=rb-2.0.0&amp;w=680&amp;fit=max&amp;v=1557931553&amp;auto=format&amp;gif-q=50&amp;q=92&amp;s=5ed3bb6826b8913305580978ebd4152e\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T03:09:53-07:00","id":1314025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1245406-pirates-of-pugmire?p=1313968#post1313968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why this one isn't attracting people as quickly as the others did though. Monarchies and Pugmire both blew past $40k in their first day. Three days in and Pirates just hit $20k.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not the only factor? There's the lack of swag. If you assume most people that are going to back Pirates already backed Pugmire and Mau... they already have most of the extras Pirates is offering. No GM screen, new Knack/Spell cards, new Calling pins, new dice... it just lowers the average backer pledge. Pugmire and Mau both had average backer pledges of ~$60, while Pirates is at ~$55.<br /> <br /> Mau also did see a fairly hefty drop off in number of backers despite still having plenty to open and finish strong.<br /> <br /> I think it's just the nature of things. It's hardly unique to Pugmire for supplements to dip below the performance of the first book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T04:10:30-07:00","id":1314034,"title":"","content":"I would gladly throw more money for Monarchies of Mau Adventure of Excellent Cats that I wanted to buy either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T05:10:48-07:00","id":1314038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1245406-pirates-of-pugmire?p=1314025#post1314025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While not the only factor? There's the lack of swag. If you assume most people that are going to back Pirates already backed Pugmire and Mau... they already have most of the extras Pirates is offering. No GM screen, new Knack/Spell cards, new Calling pins, new dice... it just lowers the average backer pledge. Pugmire and Mau both had average backer pledges of ~$60, while Pirates is at ~$55.<br /> <br /> Mau also did see a fairly hefty drop off in number of backers despite still having plenty to open and finish strong.<br /> <br /> I think it's just the nature of things. It's hardly unique to Pugmire for supplements to dip below the performance of the first book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I guess. The thing is though, Monarchies had fewer backers overall, but on day one it actually had <i>more</i> backers than Pugmire did, and finished $8000 higher. I figured Pirates would've at least funded by day 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T09:52:32-07:00","id":1314111,"title":"","content":"I appreciate that. I was just trying to point out some reasons to adjust expectations.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, lets keep in mind that success is the project getting funded at the end of the Kickstarter, not how fast it gets funded, or how many stretch goals it meets. Pirates didn't boom at launch, that's fine. It just means if we want to help get it over the line, we should be positive in our excitement to watch it get there, rather than worrying about which arc the funding pattern followed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T12:01:21-07:00","id":1314127,"title":"","content":"I'm still interested what Strech Goals are looked for ( if we even hit those... ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T21:53:49-07:00","id":1314232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1245406-pirates-of-pugmire?p=1314111#post1314111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate that. I was just trying to point out some reasons to adjust expectations.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, lets keep in mind that success is the project getting funded at the end of the Kickstarter, not how fast it gets funded, or how many stretch goals it meets. Pirates didn't boom at launch, that's fine. It just means if we want to help get it over the line, we should be positive in our excitement to watch it get there, rather than worrying about which arc the funding pattern followed.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, thing is, the funding pace has dropped pretty precipitously so far. You're right that it only matters if it hits $40k, but at this point I'm concerned about whether it will. If the pace levels out to around $700-$1000 a day, I'll be confident of that. If it drops below $500, I'll be concerned. Momentum is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T22:11:21-07:00","id":1314236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1245406-pirates-of-pugmire?p=1314232#post1314232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, thing is, the funding pace has dropped pretty precipitously so far. You're right that it only matters if it hits $40k, but at this point I'm concerned about whether it will. If the pace levels out to around $700-$1000 a day, I'll be confident of that. If it drops below $500, I'll be concerned. Momentum is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right - but we are still at about 1000$ per day now. Problem is that most funds go on from few days at start of Kickstarter and at the end - with week, two of lull in supports. In other KS it was always a drop in level of pledges, but still flowing - with this one looking like, I think it can even go to 0$ on that days. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>We will see how it will go, but without some more incentives from OPP to pay larger sums for Kickstarter </b>- like, I dunno, more PDFs bundles with adventures books or Canis Minor stuff for people to rise pledge - it maybe hard to hit 40k $, this time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-25-2019, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T04:33:09-07:00","id":1314270,"title":"","content":"We are almost 22k $ now - it's almost 2000 $ in one day. Maybe it will not be so bad, in the end... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T07:59:28-07:00","id":1314298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> 